    {
      "id": "claim_1d31412dd8b04926ba744787882e79e3",
      "statement": "A platform constraint shapes the whole architecture: a desktop web wallpaper receives no clicks and no keyboard focus (the desktop icon layer consumes mouse input, and the only official web keyboard channel would require hiding desktop icons), so every interactive capability is a window owned by the data service instead of wallpaper markup.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/adr/0001-win32-icon-manipulation.md#L3-L3",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:06ab7541cd346412ec3d2577d54eb8888fc6d5424ac95e6b9fec2603feac2b95:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/adr/0003-search-panel-service-window.md#L3-L11",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:53c6ca22f7bc60cf4082b169a2a92a47fb574a08089a25c7e4b76afd9e9fcf26:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d0121c6dd2f14fdb995fbe0b9b4f974e",
      "statement": "Because interaction never goes through the wallpaper page, the service's HTTP API stays GET-only with a permissive CORS header and no unauthenticated write channel exists; this is named as ADR-0001's main side benefit and adding a mutating route would remove it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/adr/0001-win32-icon-manipulation.md#L11-L14",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6f4ecd1720e2ab27e48fb279ac732590a8422e9e2d4b59246d182764be8a1caf:"
