        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b38a8fcae7a8464fbd71b7a6d769a2c6",
      "statement": "The wallpaper is now only the background layer: nothing in the repository builds, deploys, patches, reloads or queries it, and the window stack is background layer at the bottom, the standalone panel above it, and normal windows above the panel. The panel is a transparent, frameless, never-activatable window that calls setIgnoreMouseEvents(true) by default so clicks miss-and-fall-through to the wallpaper and desktop, and it is re-pinned with SetWindowPos(HWND_BOTTOM) because Electron has no native z-order setting for 'above the wallpaper, below every normal window'.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CONTEXT.md#L99-L109",
