    {
      "id": "claim_5f890d378ddf4393886bd4151db4cc01",
      "statement": "The only Wallpaper Engine-aware behaviour left in the code is the desktop-icon host lookup: because a dynamic-wallpaper host such as Wallpaper Engine reparents SHELLDLL_DefView under WorkerW, findDefView() probes the Progman child first and then enumerates top-level windows for a WorkerW that owns a SHELLDLL_DefView, so the panel's icon hide/restore works with either a system wallpaper or a Wallpaper Engine mount and no Wallpaper Engine process, project or setting is ever read.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/icon-carry.ts#L35-L52",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6e77f744dd41956413a4d50f5085dfabf38788033bc82e56cb206b6ae8de0a82:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7692d290a3154f78b37d0c69e97315bb",
      "statement": "On 2026-09-29 the Wallpaper Engine era was retired: the Python data service server.py with its loopback HTTP contracts, the watchdog that started it only while a Wallpaper Engine process ran, the Tk search overlay window, the Win32 real-desktop-icon arrangement chain, and the three Wallpaper Engine scripts (the DECK deployer scripts/deploy_deck.py, the patch replay scripts/apply_patch.py and the interactive rollback scripts/restore_original.py) were all removed, leaving no HTTP service and no Python in the repository; their capabilities moved into the cordis kernel services of the Electron app.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.scratch/terminal02-qoder-status/issues/01-backup-patch-infra.md#L16-L16",
